---------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT grant above covers only our own work in this repository: the PS4 port
of the kernel chains (chain_lapse.js, chain_poops.js), the per-firmware offset
tables (ps4_offsets.js), and the firmware detection, routing and offline
delivery layer.

The following bundled files are third-party work, are NOT covered by that
grant, and remain subject to the terms of their respective authors:

  core.js, mem.js, int64.js, rpc_worker.js
      SLOPKIT, by Jordy. The JavaScriptCore primitive and memory interface,
      originally written for the PlayStation 5 and rebuilt here against the
      PlayStation 4's WebKit build. All rights in the kit and its primitive
      design remain with its author.

  payload.bin
      GoldHEN, by the GoldHEN team. Redistributed unmodified.
      https://github.com/GoldHEN/GoldHEN

  patches/*.bin
      Kernel patch blobs derived from publicly published PS4 kernel patch
      sources, by their respective authors.

The underlying vulnerability research embodied in chain_lapse.js and
chain_poops.js is public work by the PS4/PS5 security research community and
is credited in README.md.

If you hold rights to any bundled component and wish its attribution or
licensing terms corrected or its inclusion withdrawn, please open an issue.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO WARRANTY - HARDWARE RISK
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software exploits memory-corruption vulnerabilities in console firmware.
It can crash the console, corrupt stored data, or leave the system requiring a
reinstall. It is provided for education and security research on hardware you
own. You run it entirely at your own risk.
